It is important to be aware that access to the document of a different tab for a different domain is highly restricted due to security policies, specifically the Same Origin Policy and the policies around Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS). 

Modern browsers prevent a webpage from making requests to a different domain than the one the webpage came from, unless the server supports CORS from the domain of the requesting website.

The usage of JavaScript execution to open a new tab and interact with it, like querying its document, is limited to the same origin due to security concerns.

As for your question, it is also important to note that Flutter is an UI toolkit that is used to build applications, and it doesn't have direct functionality to manipulate browser tabs. What you might be using is probably "flutter_web" or something similar which allows Flutter to run in a browser. However, it does not provide the same level of control over the browser as native JavaScript.

Even in JavaScript, there are limits to how you can interact with new browser tabs, especially if they are not the same domain. Trying to manipulate a website in a new browser tab (especially if the website is not your own) is generally not possible due to the browser's security restrictions. 

However, you can use `url_launcher` plugin in Flutter to direct a user to a specific page in the web browser or execute deep linking into some apps.

Here is an example:

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:url_launcher/url_launcher.dart';

void main() {
  runApp(
      MaterialApp(
        home: Scaffold(
          body: Center(
            child: RaisedButton(
              onPressed: _launchURL,
              child: Text('Show Flutter homepage'),
            ),
          ),
        ),
      )
  );
}

_launchURL() async {
  const url = 'https://www.google.com/search?q=cats';
  if (await canLaunch(url)) {
    await launch(url);
  } else {
    throw 'Could not launch $url';
  }
}
```

In this example, the app will try to open a browser tab that directly search Google for `'cats'`.

