In Java, you can program the Fibonacci series using several different methods; here's an example of a simple implementation using a `for` loop to calculate Fibonacci numbers:

```java
public class Fibonacci {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 10; // You can set the number of terms you want to print
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            System.out.println(fibonacci(i));
        }
    }

    public static int fibonacci(int n) {
        if (n <= 1) {
            return n;
        }
        int fib = 1;
        int prevFib = 1;
        for (int i = 2; i < n; i++) {
            int temp = fib;
            fib += prevFib;
            prevFib = temp;
        }
        return fib;
    }
}
```

